#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:2
msgid ""
"esutils ([esutils](http://github.com/estools/esutils)) is utility box for"
" ECMAScript language tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:5
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:7
msgid "ast"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:9
msgid "ast.isExpression(node)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:11
msgid ""
"Returns true if `node` is an Expression as defined in ECMA262 edition 5.1"
" section [11](https://es5.github.io/#x11)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:14
msgid "ast.isStatement(node)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:16
msgid ""
"Returns true if `node` is a Statement as defined in ECMA262 edition 5.1 "
"section [12](https://es5.github.io/#x12)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:19
msgid "ast.isIterationStatement(node)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:21
msgid ""
"Returns true if `node` is an IterationStatement as defined in ECMA262 "
"edition 5.1 section [12.6](https://es5.github.io/#x12.6)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:24
msgid "ast.isSourceElement(node)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:26
msgid ""
"Returns true if `node` is a SourceElement as defined in ECMA262 edition "
"5.1 section [14](https://es5.github.io/#x14)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:29
msgid "ast.trailingStatement(node)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:31
msgid "Returns `Statement?` if `node` has trailing `Statement`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:36
msgid "When taking this `IfStatement`, returns `consequent;` statement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:38
msgid "ast.isProblematicIfStatement(node)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:40
msgid ""
"Returns true if `node` is a problematic IfStatement. If `node` is a "
"problematic `IfStatement`, `node` cannot be represented as an one on one "
"JavaScript code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:54
msgid ""
"The above node cannot be represented as a JavaScript code, since the top "
"level `else` alternate belongs to an inner `IfStatement`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:57
msgid "code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:59
msgid "code.isDecimalDigit(code)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:61
msgid "Return true if provided code is decimal digit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:63
msgid "code.isHexDigit(code)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:65
msgid "Return true if provided code is hexadecimal digit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:67
msgid "code.isOctalDigit(code)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:69
msgid "Return true if provided code is octal digit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:71
msgid "code.isWhiteSpace(code)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:73
msgid ""
"Return true if provided code is white space. White space characters are "
"formally defined in ECMA262."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:75
msgid "code.isLineTerminator(code)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:77
msgid ""
"Return true if provided code is line terminator. Line terminator "
"characters are formally defined in ECMA262."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:79
msgid "code.isIdentifierStart(code)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:81
msgid ""
"Return true if provided code can be the first character of ECMA262 "
"Identifier. They are formally defined in ECMA262."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:83
msgid "code.isIdentifierPart(code)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:85
msgid ""
"Return true if provided code can be the trailing character of ECMA262 "
"Identifier. They are formally defined in ECMA262."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:87
msgid "keyword"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:89
msgid "keyword.isKeywordES5(id, strict)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:91
msgid ""
"Returns `true` if provided identifier string is a Keyword or Future "
"Reserved Word in ECMA262 edition 5.1. They are formally defined in "
"ECMA262 sections [7.6.1.1](http://es5.github.io/#x7.6.1.1) and "
"[7.6.1.2](http://es5.github.io/#x7.6.1.2), respectively. If the `strict` "
"flag is truthy, this function additionally checks whether `id` is a "
"Keyword or Future Reserved Word under strict mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:97
msgid "keyword.isKeywordES6(id, strict)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:99
msgid ""
"Returns `true` if provided identifier string is a Keyword or Future "
"Reserved Word in ECMA262 edition 6. They are formally defined in ECMA262 "
"sections [11.6.2.1](http://ecma-international.org/ecma-262/6.0/#sec-"
"keywords) and [11.6.2.2](http://ecma-international.org/ecma-262/6.0/#sec-"
"future-reserved-words), respectively. If the `strict` flag is truthy, "
"this function additionally checks whether `id` is a Keyword or Future "
"Reserved Word under strict mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:106
msgid "keyword.isReservedWordES5(id, strict)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:108
msgid ""
"Returns `true` if provided identifier string is a Reserved Word in "
"ECMA262 edition 5.1. They are formally defined in ECMA262 section "
"[7.6.1](http://es5.github.io/#x7.6.1). If the `strict` flag is truthy, "
"this function additionally checks whether `id` is a Reserved Word under "
"strict mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:113
msgid "keyword.isReservedWordES6(id, strict)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:115
msgid ""
"Returns `true` if provided identifier string is a Reserved Word in "
"ECMA262 edition 6. They are formally defined in ECMA262 section "
"[11.6.2](http://ecma-international.org/ecma-262/6.0/#sec-reserved-words)."
" If the `strict` flag is truthy, this function additionally checks "
"whether `id` is a Reserved Word under strict mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:120
msgid "keyword.isRestrictedWord(id)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:122
msgid ""
"Returns `true` if provided identifier string is one of `eval` or "
"`arguments`. They are restricted in strict mode code throughout ECMA262 "
"edition 5.1 and in ECMA262 edition 6 section [12.1.1](http://ecma-"
"international.org/ecma-262/6.0/#sec-identifiers-static-semantics-early-"
"errors)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:126
msgid "keyword.isIdentifierNameES5(id)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:128
msgid ""
"Return true if provided identifier string is an IdentifierName as "
"specified in ECMA262 edition 5.1 section "
"[7.6](https://es5.github.io/#x7.6)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:131
msgid "keyword.isIdentifierNameES6(id)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:133
msgid ""
"Return true if provided identifier string is an IdentifierName as "
"specified in ECMA262 edition 6 section [11.6](http://ecma-"
"international.org/ecma-262/6.0/#sec-names-and-keywords)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:136
msgid "keyword.isIdentifierES5(id, strict)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:138
msgid ""
"Return true if provided identifier string is an Identifier as specified "
"in ECMA262 edition 5.1 section [7.6](https://es5.github.io/#x7.6). If the"
" `strict` flag is truthy, this function additionally checks whether `id` "
"is an Identifier under strict mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:143
msgid "keyword.isIdentifierES6(id, strict)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/esutils_README.md:145
msgid ""
"Return true if provided identifier string is an Identifier as specified "
"in ECMA262 edition 6 section [12.1](http://ecma-"
"international.org/ecma-262/6.0/#sec-identifiers). If the `strict` flag is"
" truthy, this function additionally checks whether `id` is an Identifier "
"under strict mode."
msgstr ""

